{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the whole S1 head at 9b428613, tree a7789185, for request 449c58c7 and review request 154f2502. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for `examples/repo-in-ai/runbook.md` and the note only. The code, tests and evidence need no change for this verdict, so a documents-only tail needs no new gate.\n\nThe third room is good evidence, and the production changes hold. The runbook is what fails. It is the witness script, the planner runs it for the real room, and it misstates what binds a run to its room and what stops one.\n\n## Changes I request\n\n1. A deployment during a run strands that run. The note says that a later deployment makes the script stop \"until the input names it\". That is false for a run in progress. `checkDeployment` in `plan.ts` requires the input's `deploymentVersion` to equal the live version on every invocation, including `check`. `bindPlan` refuses any change to the retained plan, and that plan holds `deploymentVersion`. So after a redeploy, the old input fails at `/health` and the new input fails with \"different setup plan\". Correct the note, and say in the runbook: no Worker deployment between the first phase and the last, and a deployment in that window leaves no `check` or `continue` path. The planner owns deployments, so a stated rule is enough here.\n\n2. `name` names nothing at the service. `walkClaim` uses it only in output text, and the repository's name comes from the mint reply. Other than that, `plan.name` appears only in the Change title. `runbook.md:3` says that the script \"creates the room named repo-in-ai\", and the note gives a \"Room name\". Say what is true: the home directory binds a run to its room, `name` is a local label, and a run with a new home creates another room. The request asks you to name the room S2 to S9 use. Name it by its label and say that its references come from the run.\n\n3. State the source condition. `verify-seed` compares the clone with the retained candidate, and only `build-seed` reads `task-list/`. `loadTaskList` reads the working tree, although its comment says \"committed\". An uncommitted edit before `build-seed` still ends with every phase at exit 0. The third room isn't affected, because its receipts show the source bytes unchanged at 4b9e1a89. Add a precondition: run from a clean checkout at the reviewed commit, and keep that checkout unchanged until `verify-seed`.\n\n4. Say what closes the witness. `released` needs only `release`, and `release` needs only `hold`. `verify-seed`, `clone-verify`, `members`, `roles-after` and `rules` aren't prerequisites of any final phase. `all` enforces the order, but a single-phase run doesn't, and `all` has never closed. Say that the witness closes only when every phase in `setupPhases` has exited 0 or has completed by the stated `continue` route, and name the receipts to read.\n\n5. Correct the commands:\n   - The runbook leads with `--phase all`, but the note says that `all` has never closed and the third room ran one phase per command. Lead with the route that ran.\n   - \"Creation through first-key\" doesn't describe 42 phases.\n   - The `--diagnostics` parent must already exist, and a path holding `.config` is refused.\n   - A failure under `all` prints \"Use check\", but `--phase all --mode check` is refused. Name the phase to check.\n\n## Your six points\n\n1. I accept replacing the note. All four sealed units rerun clean at the digests the note names, and no file in them is writable. The note's evidence directory also verifies: 6 manifest rows match, 38 files with none writable, `SHA256SUMS` digest 6486a888.\n\n2. I accept this reading. In the projection, the five lists read the same before and after, and the role acts were accepted. `preservesActions` adds nothing beside the exact equality, and that equality is what holds.\n\n3. The limit is stated correctly and it needs an owner. Enrollment stopped at `invitation-result`, cause `unknown`, once in the third room and once in the second. No request owns it, and the real room can hit it. See the planner's items below.\n\n4. I accept the fresh clone at the published commit. It compares paths, modes and bytes, which is stronger than a pull that could rest on earlier local state. The note states the substitution.\n\n5. I accept `s1r3-project.mts`. It reads retained records after the run and signs nothing. I read its output, and that output holds no key or link.\n\n6. I accept this. The retained reason is `unauthorized`, and the check is on the same manifest that the owner reviews. It doesn't show which guard refused, and the done-when doesn't need that.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The gate at 42099ef1, tree efc2ec6e, exits 0: Plain 3,236 with one skip, Native 900 with two skips. From there to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` of 074255e8 and this head gives this head's tree.\n- The third room's receipts show 44 captures: exit 0 except `enrol-checker` `new` and `check`, and that phase's `continue` exits 0. From 4b9e1a89 to the checkpoint, nothing under `packages/cli` or `packages/client` changes, and in the example only the runbook and `agents.md` change. So I carry the third room's result to this source, with the limit that it ran on Worker da13242c.\n- I ran each once: `checker-key-invitation.test.ts` and `invitations.test.ts`, 13 of 13, and `security-entry-points.test.mjs`, 10 of 10. `check-commit-messages` checks 17 with 0 flagged, `git diff --check` is clean, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nI read the production diff in `packages/cli` and `packages/client`. Checker issuance has its own closed input and tag, and it can't reach person issuance or reuse an agent's original. A checker holds no controller, and the code verifies this at issue and at enrol. `cloneRetained` signs nothing, and `readTokenReceipt` binds the retained receipt to the destination and to the signed request.\n\nAn independent reader, which I gave the code without my conclusions, read the example's engines. I checked findings 1 to 5 above against the source. I did not check each of its other readings. It found no double signature, and it found the resume paths reuse retained originals, the secrets stay in private files, and stdout and diagnostics hold only fixed fields. It read only part of `enrolKey` and of `issueRetainedInvitation`, and it didn't read the tests or `task-list/`. I ran no live act.\n\n## Not blocking\n\n- `flushPrivateFile` syncs only the immediate parent directory, so a power loss could drop a home entry after `found` went out, and `owner --mode new` would then sign a new key and a new room. This depends on the filesystem, and neither of us tested it. Name it in the limits.\n- A wrong `providerOrigin` is caught only after the one-time credential is spent, and that stop is permanent. The runbook should say to check the input's origin first.\n- Several checks in the setup path can't fail, for example `identities.ts:355` and `workspace.ts:115`. They do no harm.\n\n## For the planner\n\n- Own the enrollment stop with a request, or say that you accept it as a stated limit. Two live stops with cause `unknown` are enough that the real room may meet one.\n- This script hasn't met a Worker later than 112eff12. The real run comes after the post-J4 deployment, so the script meets S4, S5, S6 and later landings there for the first time.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved in substance. The script uses the existing Register and the J4 definitions, and it changes no service default.\n- Security: approved in substance. No authority widens, and checker issuance stays separate. The verdict waits on the runbook.\n- Simplification: no objection. The redundant checks can go in a later change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66272e8a85b3ad076af1e306e51349d3f28199f2","binding":"assigned","head":"9b428613a49a14b1cd444b7484f66a98a34ebe64","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc7054c139f3a78aca98a789dcff8d909bca8337\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a90580e1d205fe7790871c11fc1012b4ec9794b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41a0daa64b4d6f53b3085b12c1fbcb1301e1e77d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}